course: dictionary
lesson: 10419
title: Three legs, one steady stand
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tripod is a stand with three legs, and three legs keep things steady even when the ground is bumpy. «Stop-motion looks jumpy if the camera moves, so animators fix the camera on a stand called a tripod.» The stand stops the camera from shaking, so the photos stay clear.
explain: Look inside the word for clues. Tri means three, as in tricycle, and pod means foot. So a tripod has three feet. When you meet a new word, look for a part you already know.
explain: The context tells you which kind of tripod is meant. In photography it holds a camera. In science it holds a dish or a beaker over a flame. Always check your meaning against the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: A tripod is a stand with three legs.
fact: Tripod can mean a camera stand, a three-legged stand for holding a dish or beaker over a Bunsen burner, or any object or creature with three legs.
fact: Three points always sit flat, so a tripod stays steady even on bumpy ground.
fact: Tri means three and pod means foot, so tripod means three feet.
fact: In «The War of the Worlds», the alien machines are called tripods because they have three legs.
exercise: «Stop-motion looks jumpy if the camera moves, so animators fix the camera on a stand called a tripod.» What is a tripod in this sentence? | A three-wheeled bike | A camera with three lenses | *A stand with three legs for holding a camera steady | A tall ladder for reaching high shelves
exercise: What does tri- mean in tripod? | Round | Two | *Three | One hundred
exercise: Why is a tripod useful on bumpy ground? | Its legs bend to fit any shape | *Three points always sit flat | It is made of soft wood | It has more legs than a table
test: In a science lab, what might a tripod hold above a Bunsen burner? | A football | A camera | *A dish or beaker | A pair of shoes
test: In «The War of the Worlds», the alien machines are tripods. What does tripod mean there? | A stand for holding a camera | A three-legged race | A small round table | *Any object or creature with three legs
exam: Which word means a stand with three legs? | Tricycle | *Tripod | Triangle | Tripe
